search\nFind a research unit\nOur research community\nFacilities and equipment\nOur impact\nResearch outputs\nResearch excellence framework (REF)\nCollaboration: innovation and growth\nOur partners\nInnovation assets and capabilities\nKnowledge Exchange Framework (KEF)\nContact us\nPostgraduate research\nDoctoral Training\nFellowships\nResearch environment\nResearcher support\nResearch news\nOriginal Ideas podcast\nClose\nBack\nGlobal Liverpool\nPartnerships\nStrategic partners\nGlobal networks\nTransnational education partners\nCollaborate with us\nGlobal study opportunities\nStudy abroad\nStudy in Liverpool\nStudy in China\nStudy in India\nAchievements and rankings\nOur global city\nSustainability\nOur global team\nLeadership team\nGlobal contacts\nOur global community\nClose\nBack\nAbout us\nThe University\nOur history\nStrategy and vision\nPeople and culture\nRankings and reputation\nReports, policies and governance documents\nOur structure\nWork at Liverpool\nOur city, our inspiration\nDiscover Liverpool\nOur commitment to the Liverpool City Region\nProfessional Services\nIT Services\nHuman Resources\nLegal\nOur campus\nCampus facilities\nLibraries\nSports facilities\nSustainability\nEquality, diversity and inclusion\nNews\nEvents\nLiverpool Literary Festival\nHire an event space\nVisit us\nMuseums and Collections\nCar parking\nContact us\nNews\nJobs\nDonate\nA-Z\nAlumni\nStaff\nStudents\nSearch the site\nPostgraduate research\nAlso in this section\nMore\nResearch opportunities\nResearch degrees explained\nPhD fees and funding\nAlternative sources of funding\nWorking alongside your research degree\nHow to apply\nHow to write a research proposal\nWhy Liverpool?\nMeet our postgraduate researchers\nCareers and professional development\nResearch support\nPostgraduate Research Experience Team (PRET)\nPGR Development Hub\nPostgraduate research events\nContact us\nAlso in this section\nMore\nHow to write a research proposal\nhome\nStudy\nPostgraduate research\nHow to apply\nHow to apply\nTo apply for a postgraduate research degree or project, you'll need to complete our online application form via the University of Liverpool Application Portal.\nYou should apply as early as possible if you're also applying for funding, or if you need to secure a UK visa. Visit the GOV.UK website to check if you need a UK visa.\n1. Find a research degree or research project\nBrowse our research degrees and research projects. Find a route that matches your funding requirements and research interests.\n2. Contact potential supervisors\nIt\u2019s useful to contact potential supervisors before you make your application. This gives you the chance to discuss their availability and your proposed research. More importantly, it gives you the opportunity to decide if they\u2019d be a good fit for you.\nIf supervisors aren't listed on the research degree page or research project page that interests you, you can find potential supervisors by browsing:\nOur people search\nOur supervisor search on FindaPhD\nOur staff\u2019s research on GoogleScholar.\n3. Prepare your application documents\nYou may need the following documents to complete your online application. You should read the application guidance for your chosen course/research opportunity carefully, as required documents may differ:\nA research proposal (this should cover the research you\u2019d like to undertake)\nUniversity transcripts\u202fand degree certificates to date\nPassport details\u202f (international applicants only)\nEnglish language certificates (international applicants only)\nA personal statement\nA curriculum vitae (CV)\nContact details for two proposed supervisors\nNames and contact details of two referees.\n4. Apply\nFinally, register and apply online. Please note: we don't list research projects in the online application portal. If you\u2019re applying for a research project, your proposed supervisor(s) or the relevant administration team can tell you which programme you should complete your online application for. You can find contact details on the relevant project page.\nYou'll receive an email acknowledgment once you've submitted your application. All submissions are considered thoroughly and carefully, so there may be a delay in receiving a decision on your application. If further documents are required in order for a decision to be made, the relevant postgraduate administration team will contact you via email.\nApply online\nRelated content\nHow to write a research proposal\nPhD fees and funding\nContact us\nWebsite footer\nInformation for\nCurrent students\nCurrent staff\nProspective students\nBusinesses and partners\nResearchers\nMedia\nStudy at Liverpool\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate taught\nPostgraduate research\nOnline courses\nCPD\nContinuing education\nInternational students\nQuick links\nJobs at Liverpool\nLibrary\nSport at Liverpool\nFind a researcher\nAlumni\nOur departments and faculties\nAll subjects\nContact us\nUniversity of Liverpool\nFoundation Building\nBrownlow Hill\nLiverpool\nL69 7ZX\nTelephone\n+44 (0) 151 794 2000\nContact us\nMaps and directions\nVisit us\nPart of the Russell Group\nAccessibility\nFreedom of information\nCookie information\nData Protection\nModern slavery statement\nTerms and Conditions\nCharitable status\n\u00a9 University of Liverpool", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/postgraduate-research/how-to-apply/#main-content"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/undergraduate/"], ["Postgraduate", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/postgraduate-taught/"], ["PhD", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/study/postgraduate-research/"], ["Accommodation", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/accommodation/"], ["Research", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/research/"], ["International students", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/international/"], ["A-Z index", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/a-z/"], ["UK", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/"], ["China", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/xjtlu/"], ["India", "https://w